# Plan vs build models

Plan/spec/review/judgment = Claude Opus 5.5 (`claude-opus-5-5`), never Fable. Build/typing = Grok
4.7 (`grok-4.7-high`, never `auto`) via `cursor-agent`, or Sonnet 5.5 when Grok fails or is over
its daily cap. UI is written by the Opus 5.5 session itself. Details: `AGENTS.md` → "Model
tiering".

**In an interactive Cursor session (this is Grok):**

- Asked to **propose, plan, audit, or design** a change: do not write the plan yourself. Launch a
  Task subagent on an Opus 5.5 thinking model. Implement only after that plan exists and the user
  accepts it.
- Asked to **implement** something already decided (including "take this out", "do what we just
  agreed"): implement it here. Do not spawn Opus to type the code.

Scheduled jobs pin their own IDs (`plans/agent-loops.md`). The Grok → Sonnet fallback is the only
sanctioned switch; never move a plan/review job off Opus 5.5 or the builder to `auto`.
